## 5. Typography

Lettering is bold, round, and bouncy. It should feel like hand-cut letters on a poster.

### 5.1 Typefaces

| Role | Typeface | Weight | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| Display (titles, wordmark, big numbers) | **Lilita One** | Regular (only weight) | Chunky, rounded, bubbly. Use with a 3 px `ink` text-stroke and a hard 3 px offset shadow for the wordmark |
| Headings (screen titles, card titles) | **Fredoka** | 600–700 | Soft, rounded, friendly |
| UI and body | **Nunito** | 600 for labels, 700 for buttons, 400–500 for body | Very readable at small sizes |
| Scores and numbers | **Lilita One** | Regular | Big, bold, instantly scannable |
| Board initials | **Lilita One** | Regular | Inside claimed boxes |

Load from Google Fonts. Do not use system fonts for display text.

### 5.2 Type scale (sp)

| Token | Size | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `display.xl` | 56 | Wordmark, results winner name |
| `display.l` | 40 | Screen titles on hero screens |
| `display.m` | 28 | Section titles, big scores |
| `heading` | 22 | Card titles |
| `body.l` | 17 | Primary body text |
| `body.m` | 15 | Default body and labels |
| `caption` | 12 | Timestamps, meta |

Minimum body size is 15 sp.

### 5.3 Typography treatments
- **Chunky title:** Lilita One, `ink` fill, 3 px `ink` outline via `paint-order: stroke fill`, with a hard 0 blur, 3 px offset shadow in `brand.honey` or a color matched to the screen.
- **Score numbers:** Lilita One, large, with a small label in Nunito 600 above.
- **Button text:** Nunito 700, uppercase only on primary actions, letter-spacing 0.5 px. Other buttons use sentence case.
- Do not set body text in Lilita One. It is for display only.

